---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="What Linx, the Linx app and linxpbx.com do with your information.">
  <section class="container prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated 7 October 2026.</p>

    <h2>Linx is software you run yourself</h2>
    <p>Linx is a phone system you install on your own server. Your calls, voicemail, call history, contacts and settings stay on that server, under the control of whoever runs it. The Linx project has no copy of them, no account with you, and no way to see them.</p>

    <h2>The iPhone and iPad app</h2>
    <p>The Linx app connects only to the Linx server it's set up with. It collects no data for us: no analytics, no advertising, no tracking. To ring when the phone is asleep, your server sends a notification through Apple's push service; it carries only the call's id, the caller's number and the time, using the server owner's own Apple key. Everything else goes between the app and your server, encrypted.</p>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>linxpbx.com sets no cookies and uses no analytics or advertising. It's served by Cloudflare, which, like any web host, sees your IP address and the pages you request in order to deliver them and protect the site.</p>

    <h2>Asking to test the app</h2>
    <p>If you ask to test the app on our <a href="/beta">TestFlight page</a>, your name, email and note are emailed to the project's owner so they can decide. They aren't stored on this website. If you're approved, your name and email are given to Apple so TestFlight can send you the invitation; Apple's own privacy policy then applies. The page uses Cloudflare Turnstile to check you're a person, which doesn't use cookies to track you.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about privacy: open an issue on <a href="https://github.com/linxpbx/linx/issues" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>.</p>
  </section>
  <style>
    .prose { max-width: 760px; padding-top: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem); }
    .prose h2 { font-size: 1.3rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
    .updated { color: var(--fg-faint); font-size: 0.9rem; }
  </style>
</Base>
